WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.435 --> 00:00:03.813
- She's an American actress,
model, and businesswoman.

00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:05.322
Her Honest Company business,

00:00:05.322 --> 00:00:09.657
has become a huge success
with a $1 billion valuation.

00:00:09.657 --> 00:00:13.266
She has an estimated net
worth of over $200 million.

00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:14.598
She's Jessica Alba,

00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:17.324
and here are her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:17.324 --> 00:00:20.460
(jet engine)

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.573
When I was a kid, my parents said,

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:24.608
anything that you want you can achieve,

00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:27.132
you just have to work
really, really hard for it.

00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:28.920
I spent a lot of time in my head,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.799
fantasizing about being a super hero,

00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:33.479
and about being somebody else.

00:00:33.479 --> 00:00:36.934
And what would it be like to
live someone else's reality?

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:40.735
There weren't so many women
that were action stars.

00:00:40.735 --> 00:00:42.852
I thought that it would be really cool

00:00:42.852 --> 00:00:44.949
to be able to kick some butt.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:46.804
The resistance that anybody has,

00:00:46.804 --> 00:00:48.649
whether you're a man or a woman,

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:53.270
to your idea should do
nothing but drive you forward.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:57.020
And force you to really
hone in on your idea,

00:00:58.457 --> 00:00:59.741
and give you energy.

00:00:59.741 --> 00:01:03.115
And if it actually holds you back,

00:01:03.115 --> 00:01:05.457
and makes you second guess yourself,

00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:08.115
then maybe you shouldn't be doing it.

00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:11.125
Creating a business is impossible,

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:13.483
at times it feels impossible,

00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:17.650
and so you really have to be
just so passionate about it,

00:01:18.846 --> 00:01:22.263
and really don't take no for an answer.

00:01:22.263 --> 00:01:25.264
If anything can deviate
you from your path,

00:01:25.264 --> 00:01:28.541
then maybe it's not
necessarily the right one.

00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:32.221
So make sure it's what you want it to be.

00:01:32.221 --> 00:01:37.192
Stay focused, and allow all
that resistance along the way,

00:01:37.192 --> 00:01:41.323
to really give you energy
and fuel your engine

00:01:41.323 --> 00:01:43.287
to move forward.

00:01:43.287 --> 00:01:44.251
I always help.

00:01:44.251 --> 00:01:47.662
You know, I think I do unto others

00:01:47.662 --> 00:01:51.071
what I would want them to do
unto me, at the end of the day.

00:01:51.071 --> 00:01:53.166
My parents always taught me that.

00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:57.113
And so I treat people the
way I want to be treated.

00:01:57.113 --> 00:02:00.565
And that's kind of the
standards that I live by.

00:02:00.565 --> 00:02:04.565
You know, we have direct
access to our customer.

00:02:06.861 --> 00:02:09.232
Because I'm into social media,

00:02:09.232 --> 00:02:11.623
and I want to hear feedback from parents,

00:02:11.623 --> 00:02:13.228
how they like our products,

00:02:13.228 --> 00:02:15.447
and what they would like to change,

00:02:15.447 --> 00:02:19.519
and how they would like to
innovate on these products.

00:02:19.519 --> 00:02:22.436
To have a brand that's for parents,

00:02:23.574 --> 00:02:24.773
is made by parents,

00:02:24.773 --> 00:02:26.808
and then we're listening to parents

00:02:26.808 --> 00:02:30.292
on how to change and grow, and evolve.

00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:34.328
I think the big differentiator
with our company

00:02:34.328 --> 00:02:36.625
versus the other companies out there,

00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:40.673
is they spend millions
and millions of dollars

00:02:40.673 --> 00:02:44.283
on product development to
make a product for one cent.

00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:47.656
They want to make the cheapest
product as humanly possible,

00:02:47.656 --> 00:02:51.823
and they don't really look
at the health ramifications

00:02:52.792 --> 00:02:54.099
or the healthiness of it.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:57.330
It's really just how
cheap, and high volume.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.739
And we're exactly the opposite.

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:03.159
And so we spend a lot of
money on product development,

00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:06.171
on high performance, on
the best ingredients,

00:03:06.171 --> 00:03:07.586
the healthiest ingredients.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:10.665
But really honing in on performance.

00:03:10.665 --> 00:03:14.145
I think it's important for there to be,

00:03:14.145 --> 00:03:17.031
really no bureaucracy here.

00:03:17.031 --> 00:03:18.781
Everyone has a voice.

00:03:19.945 --> 00:03:24.217
I encourage people to be
creative and inspired.

00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:26.713
No matter what position you're in here,

00:03:26.713 --> 00:03:28.629
everyone has an equal playing field

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:32.169
in making this company the
best company it can be.

00:03:32.169 --> 00:03:35.482
So whether it's someone in our warehouse,

00:03:35.482 --> 00:03:38.045
who is a fantastic artist,

00:03:38.045 --> 00:03:41.962
and he brings his art to
some of our customers.

00:03:44.059 --> 00:03:48.165
He spent 12 hours this one
employee of ours, Dylan,

00:03:48.165 --> 00:03:49.287
he's a rock star.

00:03:49.287 --> 00:03:53.105
And he spent 12 hours
customizing a box a month

00:03:53.105 --> 00:03:55.349
for one of our customers.

00:03:55.349 --> 00:03:57.629
Whether he's doing a dinosaur or a robot,

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:00.846
whatever if is, we want to bring delight

00:04:00.846 --> 00:04:04.788
and happiness to people
outside, our customers,

00:04:04.788 --> 00:04:06.684
but also inside.

00:04:06.684 --> 00:04:08.140
So we do whatever we can.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.702
We have karaoke nights.

00:04:10.702 --> 00:04:13.160
We have what do you think would be

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.472
the best thing in the whole world,

00:04:14.472 --> 00:04:17.273
that you would want
this company to do days.

00:04:17.273 --> 00:04:19.216
Which is everyday.

00:04:19.216 --> 00:04:22.037
And you know, I'm an actor,
so I really approach it

00:04:22.037 --> 00:04:26.037
from a more playful,
creative kind of mentality.

00:04:27.048 --> 00:04:30.043
And I really want people to
be inspired, and have fun.

00:04:30.043 --> 00:04:34.274
And I want them to really
challenge themselves,

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.026
to push the limits.

00:04:36.026 --> 00:04:40.595
Well I was 12, so I didn't
really have any idea

00:04:40.595 --> 00:04:43.597
of anything other than what I was doing.

00:04:43.597 --> 00:04:47.764
And I just hustled, and I
tried to be professional,

00:04:48.914 --> 00:04:50.801
and tried to learn from my mistakes,

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:55.207
and just try to stay two
steps ahead of everyone

00:04:55.207 --> 00:04:56.727
and get those jobs.

00:04:56.727 --> 00:04:58.097
Did you know that at that age

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.867
that this is what you want to
do for the rest of your life?

00:04:59.867 --> 00:05:00.988
Because a lot of people
will get these jobs

00:05:00.988 --> 00:05:01.821
when they're young,

00:05:01.821 --> 00:05:02.654
and they think okay this is good

00:05:02.654 --> 00:05:04.305
for high school or whatever.

00:05:04.305 --> 00:05:05.613
But when did you make that decision

00:05:05.613 --> 00:05:08.284
this is going to be a life decision?

00:05:08.284 --> 00:05:09.927
When I got Dark Angel.

00:05:09.927 --> 00:05:13.854
Because I didn't want to be
a struggling professional

00:05:13.854 --> 00:05:15.094
in anything.

00:05:15.094 --> 00:05:18.906
My parents financially,
they didn't have a lot,

00:05:18.906 --> 00:05:20.412
and they struggled a lot.

00:05:20.412 --> 00:05:21.626
And so I just wanted to make sure

00:05:21.626 --> 00:05:23.240
that I was going to be set,

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.540
and I wasn't going to struggle.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.649
And when I got Dark Angel, that was like,

00:05:26.649 --> 00:05:30.035
okay maybe I can do this for a living.

00:05:30.035 --> 00:05:32.928
And maybe it could be
a real career for me.

00:05:32.928 --> 00:05:35.111
Being intuitive is important.

00:05:35.111 --> 00:05:38.884
And then surround yourself
with really smart,

00:05:38.884 --> 00:05:42.292
business people that can
support your weaknesses.

00:05:42.292 --> 00:05:44.059
Know what they are.

00:05:44.059 --> 00:05:47.059
I know I don't know how to
create an e-commerce platform.

00:05:47.059 --> 00:05:49.069
I'm well aware of that.

00:05:49.069 --> 00:05:52.527
So I surrounded myself
with people who can,

00:05:52.527 --> 00:05:54.110
and who do do that.

00:05:55.206 --> 00:05:58.623
And then as far as mentors go, countless.

00:05:59.775 --> 00:06:04.302
I was not shy about making
phone calls to many people.

00:06:04.302 --> 00:06:07.122
I've been fortunate
enough to know people like

00:06:07.122 --> 00:06:10.039
Tory Burch, and Di von Fürstenberg.

00:06:10.991 --> 00:06:15.508
And they got lots of emails
and phone calls from me

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.864
along the way, with tears in my eyes,

00:06:17.864 --> 00:06:20.229
saying I don't know if this is possible,

00:06:20.229 --> 00:06:22.274
why is everyone telling me no?

00:06:22.274 --> 00:06:23.571
What do I do?

00:06:23.571 --> 00:06:26.855
What does it even mean
to get venture capitol?

00:06:26.855 --> 00:06:28.520
What is venture capitol?

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.412
What's a board?

00:06:29.412 --> 00:06:31.876
Like I just didn't know
all these business terms.

00:06:31.876 --> 00:06:35.250
And so they helped me understand it.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.952
I needed people telling me no.

00:06:36.952 --> 00:06:40.155
I needed people to not get
it, and look at me cross-eyed,

00:06:40.155 --> 00:06:44.628
for me to really figure out
exactly what I was going to do,

00:06:44.628 --> 00:06:46.218
and how I was going to do it.

00:06:46.218 --> 00:06:47.916
It's something that I had to
learn as a woman in business,

00:06:47.916 --> 00:06:49.749
is A, to ask for help.

00:06:51.742 --> 00:06:54.575
And to not be afraid of criticism.

00:06:58.007 --> 00:07:00.533
And when you don't know what to do,

00:07:00.533 --> 00:07:03.450
to be okay with not knowing, but learning.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.064
And also to not be
defined by your mistakes.

00:07:06.064 --> 00:07:08.177
There's challenges, there's roadblocks,

00:07:08.177 --> 00:07:10.267
there's mountains.

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:12.833
And you just have to figure it out.

00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:15.719
You just have to be malleable.

00:07:15.719 --> 00:07:18.863
You have to surround yourself
with really smart people.

00:07:18.863 --> 00:07:21.553
And I didn't think I was
smart for a really long time.

00:07:21.553 --> 00:07:22.695
- Do you think you're smart now?

00:07:22.695 --> 00:07:24.442
- Yeah, I think I'm--

00:07:24.442 --> 00:07:25.384
- We agree.

00:07:25.384 --> 00:07:29.766
- You know I'm not the
smartest, but I try.

00:07:29.766 --> 00:07:33.236
I had this idea on how a
family brand can be built,

00:07:33.236 --> 00:07:35.787
that was honest and convenient.

00:07:35.787 --> 00:07:38.543
The thing that drove
me was wanting the best

00:07:38.543 --> 00:07:41.447
and setting the bar really, really high.

00:07:41.447 --> 00:07:43.455
There's always a way to do it better.

00:07:43.455 --> 00:07:45.494
People looked at me like I was nuts.

00:07:45.494 --> 00:07:48.018
You want to do all of this?

00:07:48.018 --> 00:07:49.727
It's too big of an idea.

00:07:49.727 --> 00:07:51.190
Why don't you just do an endorsement?

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:52.535
It would just be so much easier.

00:07:52.535 --> 00:07:54.382
And it was about money for them.

00:07:54.382 --> 00:07:56.614
And I was like, but this
isn't about money for me.

00:07:56.614 --> 00:07:59.118
I needed to do this for my daughter,

00:07:59.118 --> 00:08:01.380
I needed to do this for other families.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.969
There was no way that I could give up

00:08:02.969 --> 00:08:04.886
until I gave it my all.

00:08:06.007 --> 00:08:07.352
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:08:07.352 --> 00:08:10.789
I made this video because
Robin Nicole Songwriter

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:11.961
asked me to.

00:08:11.961 --> 00:08:13.261
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:08:13.261 --> 00:08:14.905
that you want me to profile next,

00:08:14.905 --> 00:08:16.269
leave it in the comments below,

00:08:16.269 --> 00:08:17.691
and I'll see what I can do.

00:08:17.691 --> 00:08:19.955
I'd also love to know
which of Jessica Alba's

00:08:19.955 --> 00:08:22.026
top 10 rules meant the most to you;

00:08:22.026 --> 00:08:23.538
you're going to take some action on.

00:08:23.538 --> 00:08:24.538
Leave it in the comments,

00:08:24.538 --> 00:08:26.078
and I'm going to join the discussion.

00:08:26.078 --> 00:08:27.552
Thank you so much for watching,

00:08:27.552 --> 00:08:28.896
continue to believe,

00:08:28.896 --> 00:08:30.719
and we'll see you soon.

00:08:30.719 --> 00:08:32.739
(jet engine)

